{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Conditional_Probability)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Conditional Probability)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(by_Interstigation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (by Interstigation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a particular game, each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> players rolls a standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17be6cd0c6036497941f1416c6be49264147c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6{ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided die. The winner is the player who rolls the highest number. If there is a tie for the highest roll, those involved in the tie will roll again and this process will continue until one player wins. Hugo is one of the players in this game. What is the probability that Hugo's first roll was a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> given that he won the game?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81c941723dab7afeeea385ede6088bec9df1b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\textbf{A})\\: \\frac{61}{216}\\qquad(\\textbf{B}) \\: \\frac{367}{1296}\\qquad(\\textbf{C}) \\: \\frac{41}{144}\\qquad(\\textbf{D}) \\: \\frac{185}{648}\\qquad(\\textbf{E}) \\: \\frac{11}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"451\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the events <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> - Hugo wins.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> - Hugo's first roll is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> - The highest number any player rolls on their first turn is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The desired probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a27cd63b2ab1d6d86976ed9a6162e1414ca924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(A|H)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />.  In all games Hugo wins, the number Hugo rolls on his first turn must equal the highest number any player rolls on their first turn, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/7/4778d30c5021fc0fd889bb150992d3915aed9dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(A|H) = P(B|H)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />.  By symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are independent events and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b0808862a4095dd4e225e95f8238db4f210387f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(B|H) = P(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p>Define the random variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> as the highest number any player rolls on their first turn.  \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80319015a41aaa1546edc33cb10f8dc846c5e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(A|H) = P(B) = P(X = 5) = P(X \\leq 5) - P(X \\leq 4) = \\left(\\frac56\\right)^4-\\left(\\frac46\\right)^4=\\frac{5^4-4^4}{6^4}=\\frac{369}{1296}=\\boxed{(\\textbf{C}) \\: \\frac{41}{144}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"830\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Conditional_Probability.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Conditional_Probability)\">Solution 2 (Conditional Probability)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Conditional Probability)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The conditional probability formula states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5547c321560cc54c123ab85b1b34ab7052714f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(A|B) = \\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"169\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df4d239d30a0d8fecc62689ecd19dd1a979261e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A|B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> means A given B and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b314c700ed7771145eb687d83a73d437a66de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\cap B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> means A and B. Therefore the probability that Hugo rolls a five given he won is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f7f77b3c0c9eb2116e64c0bfea13f868735de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"29\" />, where A is the probability that he rolls a five and B is the probability that he wins. In written form, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b16671c9fe6f8b2ab9c2c9718d5470c0f419e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{P(Hugo rolled a 5 given he won)}=\\frac{\\text{P(Hugo rolls a 5 and wins)}}{\\text{P(Hugo wins)}}.\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The probability that Hugo wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> by symmetry since there are four people playing and there is no bias for any one player. The probability that he gets a 5 and wins is more difficult; we will have to consider cases on how many players tie with Hugo. We consider the cases in which Hugo wins first, find the probabilities of those, and then account for the probability that Hugo rolled a 5, at the end.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7fc8bd87f70c04687e145d72c7b03b4d902f80d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 1:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> No Players Tie With Hugo\n</p><p>In this case, all other players must have numbers from 1 through four, and Hugo had a probability of 1 to win after the first round.\n</p><p>There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be028048650a6bec0546e194ef114eed0553bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{4}{6}\\right)^{3} \\cdot 1 = \\frac{8}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"117\" height=\"48\" /> chance of this happening.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331226e700ae378565242419f911b29b000845c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 2:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> One Player Ties With Hugo\n</p><p>In this case, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c325b6811c0fbc16eae753d64008e1a77bc5ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\choose 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"27\" height=\"28\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d248218df85d051b349827fce821263c5c6fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 3$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> ways to choose which other player ties with Hugo, and the probability that this happens is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455f4f0c7dcff2b418c0772d83556d4027402482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{6} \\cdot \\left(\\tfrac{4}{6}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"60\" height=\"27\" />. The probability that Hugo wins the game is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/218c6b3e76211f744168e77b8ad9822ccce27d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> because there are now two players rolling the die. \n</p><p>Therefore the total probability in this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610f4929326091001093b18b8c14c880064b2f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{4}{6}\\right)^2= \\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"160\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/949308f1d0158c4f33a3154470cc9db508bdb248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 3:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> Two Players Tie With Hugo\n</p><p>In this case, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c65582d5a3f4ed3a2d3ea55c7a466d4a1de6f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\choose 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"27\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d248218df85d051b349827fce821263c5c6fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 3$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> ways to choose which other players tie with Hugo, and the probability that this happens is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/6356c01a1cb94843c719b538a8b8adc9fc7eb4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\tfrac{1}{6}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\tfrac{4}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"60\" height=\"27\" />. The probability that Hugo wins the game is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53700c7fb5b8947273bbcdaf696719461fcb124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> because there are now three players rolling the die. \n</p><p>Therefore the total probability in this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c760d83c3840402834af9e7e6f9d2f1ac88ec186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{1}{54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"170\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced45ddc365d6b23b6cb905528dce1b8b4cd9d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 4:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> All Three Players Tie With Hugo\n</p><p>In this case, the probability that all three players tie with Hugo is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbf7b91b6c0b8dad92de6afbee6adf8d7300b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\tfrac{1}{6}\\right)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"36\" height=\"27\" />. The probability that Hugo wins the game is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84a414e9655bf25b41aebc8c9f7bcb651acf2fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" />, so the total probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576032bd2a082dc338a79411381a7425d38a0f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^3 = \\frac{1}{864}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Hugo has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability of rolling a five himself, so the total probability that Hugo rolls a 5 and wins is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5d522fe7823588f7ab689b3c378c6ec5d13925.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\frac{8}{27} + \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{54} + \\frac{1}{864}\\right) = \\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\frac{369}{864}\\right) = \\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\frac{41}{96}\\right).\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Finally, the total probability is this probability divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> which is this probability times four; the final answer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e4fd22f9234ebcbe0ac7c860e76e47eb0ac2eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\frac{41}{96}\\right) = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{41}{96} = \\frac{41}{48 \\cdot 3} = \\frac{41}{144} = \\boxed{C}.\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~KingRavi\n</p><p>~Edits by BakedPotato66, mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to refer to Hugo.\nWe use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d307bbd1badc9884ef8f01724a6e1cbf9e173a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> to denote the outcome of Hugo's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />th toss.\nWe denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the other three players.\nWe denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> the number of players among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> whose first tosses are 5.\nWe use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> to denote the winner.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a5825608d759df15094f9dfc4eb974cb749efa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P \\left( H_1 = 5 | W = H \\right) &amp; = \\frac{P \\left( H_1 = 5 , W = H \\right)}{P \\left( W = H \\right)} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{P \\left( H_1 = 5 \\right) P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right) }{P \\left( W = H \\right)} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\frac{1}{6} P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right)}{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{2}{3} P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right) . \\end{align*}\" width=\"422\" height=\"189\" />\n</p><p>Now, we compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e28e9a97f90fdd63a523e1d3ef794a3e9639c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1e4dc0a5828d6b1a9b019f4686c048ffd6f1d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp; P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4 \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4 | H_1 = 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 6 \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 6 | H_1 = 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + \\sum_{N = 1}^3 P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N  | H_1 = 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4 \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4  \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 6 \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 6 \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + \\sum_{N = 1}^3 P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 1 \\cdot P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4  \\right) + 0 \\cdot P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 6 \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + \\sum_{N = 1}^3 P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) \\\\ &amp; = P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} \\leq 4  \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\quad + \\sum_{N = 1}^3 P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 , \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) P \\left( \\max \\left\\{ A_1, B_1, C_1 \\right\\} = 5 , N \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\left( \\frac{4}{6} \\right)^3 + \\sum_{N = 1}^3 \\frac{1}{N + 1} \\cdot \\binom{3}{N} \\left( \\frac{1}{6} \\right)^N \\left( \\frac{4}{6} \\right)^{3 - N} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{41}{96} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"708\" height=\"520\" />\nThe first equality follows from the law of total probability.\nThe second equality follows from the property that Hugo's outcome is independent from other players' outcomes.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bcad244a09c788479ffb6ade5b17e8ea6dff00ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P \\left( H_1 = 5 | W = H \\right) &amp; = \\frac{2}{3} P \\left( W = H | H_1 = 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{2}{3} \\frac{41}{96} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{41}{144} , \\end{align*}\" width=\"341\" height=\"123\" />\nso the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c02e61bf8f6ed2e883608e5d9e058ec7f9e8e7cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{41}{144}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Interactive_Teaching_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=56o3DBGeBQw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=56o3DBGeBQw</a>\n</p><p>~MathkidsbyMax\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kfn0Bq1-Y5I\">https://youtu.be/kfn0Bq1-Y5I</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28by_Interstigation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(by_Interstigation)\">Video Solution 2 (by Interstigation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (by Interstigation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rFYTtzlN1Bw\">https://youtu.be/rFYTtzlN1Bw</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution 3 by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/V7yTQ8CU-JI\">https://youtu.be/V7yTQ8CU-JI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Ke